{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\nBhargav Bhatt, private communication.\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$u$", "MATH_0002": "$v$", "MATH_0003": "$v \\circ u$", "MATH_0004": "$u$", "MATH_0005": "$u \\circ v$", "MATH_0006": "$v$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-adjoint}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-left-adjoint-composed-fully-faithful}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:decf387766e0f2d4123174a431a141de6e30ee9ead986d5a60c7aec17e98e7e0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8e030b5e5c18634c66f53d14e6886302ab7c1db0cc1291bdc292f9125dddbc06", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a left adjoint to <MATH_0002> as in Definition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0003> is fully faithful, then <MATH_0004> is fully faithful.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is fully faithful, then <MATH_0006> is fully faithful.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4c4d0060e5cfe56dc513ab8180dee3f9971e7cc2e254d0aadcf4740d420a2375", "unit_id": "tag:0FWV:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u \\circ v$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\Mor(X,Y) \\to \\Mor(v(X),v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y)))\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$v$", "MATH_0007": "$u$", "MATH_0008": "$v$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\Mor(v(X), v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y))) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), Y)\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$u(v(Y)) \\to Y$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Mor(v(X), v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y)))$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7d34fde23fabb73406d42b55bd5e8d915f60bebe0a7315952a43cbe2c4a3da41", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f25355a3ba99ebdf4eb98f0b6dbf70197ea5f7805bab39e5b3d74ede5f7832fd", "source_text": "Proof of (2). Assume <MATH_0001> is fully faithful.\nSay we have <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004>.\nThen the natural composite map\n<MATH_0005>\nis a bijection, so <MATH_0006> is at least faithful. To show full faithfulness,\nwe must show that the second map above is injective.\nBut the adjunction between <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> says that\n<MATH_0009>\nis a bijection, where the first map is natural one and\nthe second map comes from the counit <MATH_0010> of the adjunction.\nSo this says that\n<MATH_0011>\nis also injective, as wanted. The proof of (1) is dual to this.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3c662d99315a0a5412c3ceaac5b6d01603249bf85ee9dda17dd917faddfb3423", "unit_id": "tag:0FWV:proof"}
